{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, it reveals simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing. Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack. The researchers designed a self-segregating molecule (NFA) that enriches at the buried interface to synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, and create a hydrophobic barrier. This approach achieved record power-conversion efficiencies of 24.84% and 21.46% on mini-modules while maintaining 96.26% efficiency after 1000h damp aging at 85±5% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation occurs at both gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack",
    "Self-segregating molecule NFA synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, and forms a hydrophobic barrier"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a rational strategy to overcome kinetic-environmental constraints in scalable flexible perovskite photovoltaics."
}

{
  "summary": "This review investigates Treg-endothelial cell interactions in cardiovascular disease pathogenesis. It examines how metabolic processes like glycolysis-lactate signaling, hypoxia, mitochondrial function, and redox balance influence immune microenvironment remodeling. The study highlights Tregs' role in suppressing inflammation and maintaining endothelial integrity while identifying metabolic interventions and multi-omics approaches for targeted therapies.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Treg-endothelial crosstalk is modulated by metabolic pathways including glycolysis-lactate signaling and hypoxic adaptation",
    "Tregs suppress inflammation and preserve endothelial barrier function in cardiovascular disease",
    "Metabolic therapies and spatial multi-omics approaches can target Treg-endoth:endothelial interactions for CVD treatment"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review provides a metabolic framework for understanding Treg-endothelial interactions in cardiovascular disease, offering potential targets for mechanistic studies and precision therapies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates factors influencing early human settlement in arid regions, focusing on the role of stone availability alongside water. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across the Rub' al Khali desert, researchers found no lithic artefacts or knappable raw materials in areas with abundant freshwater, despite 55 of 125 surveyed localities having palaeolake deposits. The results indicate that early human settlement tracked co-occurrence of water and lithic resources rather than water alone, suggesting that raw-material geology constrains dispersal patterns.",
  "key_findings": [
    "No lithic artefacts or knappable raw materials were found in 95% of surveyed areas with abundant freshwater",
    "Palaeolake deposits existed at 55 of 125 localities but settlement required both water and lithic resources",
    "Spatial modeling shows 57% of water-accessible terrain lacks knappable stone, improving site discrimination accuracy to 0.768"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that lithic resource availability, not water alone, critically constrained early human dispersal across arid landscapes, challenging existing models that prioritize hydrological factors in paleodemographic studies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study engineered a self-powered bubble motor microswarm (Butor) to isolate and profile circulating extracellular vesicles (EVs) from liquid biopsies. The system demonstrates jellyfish-like locomotion in biofluids, achieving rapid EV subtype isolation (near 90% in 10 minutes) and ultrasensitive detection at single-particle levels. It enables early non-small cell lung cancer diagnosis (94% accuracy) and improves cancer staging, treatment response monitoring, and immunotherapy prediction.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Butor microswarm achieves rapid isolation of EV subtypes in high-viscosity biofluids with 90% efficiency within 10 minutes",
    "The system enables ultrasensitive EV profiling at single-particle resolution for early non-small cell lung cancer diagnosis (94% accuracy)",
    "Butor improves cancer staging, surgical treatment response monitoring, and immunotherapy efficacy prediction in non-small cell lung cancer patients"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This approach provides an intelligent, multiplexed liquid biopsy tool for ultrasensitive cancer detection and monitoring with minimal sample preparation, advancing clinical translation of extracellular vesicle analysis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and IL-23-driven gut inflammation. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors like PRKAR1A. Deletion of Prkar1a reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice. IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and causing gut inflammation. Human ILC3s express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated by IL-23 or in inflammatory bowel disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors (PRKAR1A) in ILC3s",
    "Prkar1a deletion reduces ILC3 numbers and increases enteric infection susceptibility in mice",
    "IL-23 overproduction decreases PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3 homeostasis, revealing how IL-23 disrupts this balance to drive intestinal inflammation through PRKAR1A modulation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how maternal and early life obesity affect adaptive immune responses during childhood vaccination. Using a mouse model replicating the obesity-epidemiological link, researchers found that high-fat diet exposure during pregnancy or early life, but not adulthood, altered naive CD4+ T cell epigenetics and transcriptional profiles. This impaired T follicular helper cell differentiation and germinal center reactions to mRNA and protein vaccines. Mechanistically, epigenetic repression of A20 (Tnfaip3) was central to these defects, with pediatric A20 haploinsufficiency correlating with reduced TFH cells. The findings establish maternal and early life obesity as critical determinants of vaccine immunity during development.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Maternal and early life obesity, but not adulthood, alter naive CD4+ T cell epigenetics and transcriptional profiles",
    "High-fat diet exposure during pregnancy or early life impairs T follicular helper cell differentiation and germinal center reactions to vaccines",
    "Epigenetic repression of A20 (Tnfaip3) drives immune defects, with pediatric A20 haploinsufficiency linked to reduced TFH cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies maternal and early life obesity as key determinants of adaptive immune responses during critical developmental windows, providing mechanistic insights into how obesity programs long-term vaccine immunity deficits."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates iron's melting temperature and resistivity under Earth core pressures using microsecond pulsed Joule heating in diamond anvil cells. Over 300 reproducible melting measurements reveal a shallow melting curve, reaching 6 K/GPa and 4160 ± 80 K at 200 GPa. The findings suggest a cold core-mantle boundary (3430 K) and low adiabatic outer core heat flow (9.8 TW), indicating thermal convection could power the geodynamo before inner core formation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A shallow melting curve for iron at 200 GPa with a melting temperature of 4160 ± 80 K",
    "Inferred core-mantle boundary temperature of 3430 K",
    "Low adiabatic outer core heat flow of 9.8 TW"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides critical constraints on iron's melting behavior and resistivity at high pressures, advancing understanding of Earth's core thermal evolution and geodynamo mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility in cocatalysts between alkaline water oxidation systems and pure water splitting as a critical bottleneck. The researchers developed a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst using a multi-step incipient wetness impregnation strategy. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx system achieved stoichiometric pure water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest reported for Ta-based nitride/oxynitride photocatalysts. Mechanistic insights indicate enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and intermediate kinetics, overcoming the bottleneck.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of cocatalyst incompatibility as the critical bottleneck for stable pure water splitting over Ta3N5",
    "Development of a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst via multi-step incipient wetness impregnation",
    "Optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx achieved 0.72% apparent quantum yield at 420 nm for stoichiometric water splitting"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a key design principle for stable photocatalytic pure water splitting and provides mechanistic insights for advancing nitride and oxynitride photocatalysts."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines how FOXP3 variants disrupt regulatory T-cell function in IPEX syndrome and related disorders, comparing genetic mechanisms involving BACH2, IL2RA, STAT5B, CTLA4, or LRBA. It highlights structural and epigenetic insights, diagnostic approaches including genetic testing and immunophenotyping, and treatment strategies from HSCT to emerging cellular therapies. The study emphasizes distinguishing IPEX-like presentations from true Tregopathies and underscores the need for tailored therapeutic assessments.",
  "key_findings": [
    "FOXP3 variants impair regulatory T-cell function despite normal circulating numbers in IPEX syndrome",
    "Genetic testing and immunophenotyping are critical for diagnosis, with structural and epigenetic analyses supporting differentiation",
    "Hematopoietic stem cell transplantation remains a curative option, while emerging cellular therapies require individualized assessment"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work clarifies the molecular mechanisms underlying IPEX syndrome and related disorders, providing a framework for distinguishing functional Treg deficiencies from other immune dysregulation conditions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether brief dietary changes influence acute inflammatory responses and long-term tissue memory during disease onset. Using lean mice with acute type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a transient high-fat diet (HFD) exposure within a 4-day window exacerbates disease severity comparably to chronic obesity. HFD outside this window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window reduces inflammation. Mechanistically, HFD rapidly recruits neutrophils, which express Nlrp3 and Il1b, driving pathogenic TH17 cell activation. After recovery, a chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cell population persists, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent low-fat diet. The findings demonstrate that dietary state during a narrow temporal window can durably reprogram disease trajectory through neutrophil-NLRP3-IL-1β signaling.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure within a 4-day window exacerbates acute type 17 skin inflammation in lean mice comparably to chronic obesity",
    "HFD outside the 4-day window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during this window blunts disease amplification",
    "Neutrophil recruitment and NLRP3-IL-1β signaling drive pathogenic TH17 cell activation, with persistent tissue-resident memory T cells causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that short-lived dietary states during specific temporal windows can durably reprogram immune memory, revealing a mechanism by which transient metabolic conditions influence long-term inflammatory disease trajectories."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated mucin-responsive nanomedicine design to overcome solid tumour penetration barriers. Researchers engineered paclitaxel-conjugated micelles that disassemble in mucin-rich environments, enabling deeper tumor cell delivery. In pancreatic tumors, the mucin-responsive nanomedicine achieved 3.9-fold higher delivery than non-responsive controls and superior tumor growth inhibition compared to standard treatments.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Mucin-responsive nanomedicine disassembles in mucin-rich tumor microenvironments",
    "Enhanced tumor cell delivery (3.9-fold) in pancreatic tumors compared to non-responsive nanomedicine",
    "Superior tumor growth inhibition versus Abraxane in multiple solid tumor models"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This platform demonstrates a generalizable strategy for improving nanomedicine penetration in solid tumors by exploiting mucin-induced nanoparticle disassembly."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how fever enhances antibacterial immunity by identifying olfactory receptor 560 (OR560) as a key mediator. Using CRISPR screening and temperature modulation in mice, researchers found fever induces OR560 expression in macrophages, promoting pseudopod formation and phagocytosis of bacteria. Genetic ablation of OR560 or serum response factor impaired bacterial clearance and increased mortality, indicating OR560's critical role in fever-driven immune responses.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Fever induces OR560 expression in macrophages via serum response factor",
    "OR560 drives pseudopod formation necessary for bacterial phagocytosis",
    "Genetic deletion of OR560 or serum response factor causes defective bacterial clearance and higher mortality"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies OR560 as a pivotal molecular link between fever and antibacterial phagocytosis, revealing how host temperature signals integrate with pathogen recognition to enhance immune defense."
}

{
  "summary": "This Science journal article describes a weekly compilation of new laboratory instruments, apparatus, and materials potentially useful for researchers. The study provides a curated list of recently introduced scientific products without conducting experimental research. The main finding is the systematic listing of emerging research tools for the scientific community.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Weekly compilation of new laboratory instruments and apparatus",
    "List of recently introduced scientific materials for researchers",
    "Focus on products of potential interest to the scientific community"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This study contributes to the scientific ecosystem by facilitating access to emerging research tools through a structured, periodic update mechanism."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how 4f electron filling influences bonding evolution across the lanthanide series using structurally uniform single-atom catalysts. It reveals a dual-periodic trend in lanthanide-support and adsorbate binding energies, increasing from La to Eu and Gd to Yb. The half-filled 4f7 configuration causes a transition between Eu and Gd, with electron redistribution between 5d and 4f orbitals modulating bonding. These findings establish a 4f-electron-regulated framework for understanding lanthanide reactivity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A dual-periodic trend in lanthanide-support binding energies increases from La to Eu and Gd to Yb",
    "The half-filled 4f7 configuration induces an abrupt transition between Eu and Gd",
    "Electron redistribution between 5d and 4f orbitals modulates bonding energies across the series"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study identifies a fundamental 4f-electron-regulated bonding mechanism intrinsic to lanthanide chemistry, providing a unified framework for predicting and designing lanthanide-based catalysts."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how Ampelopsis grossedentata (AG) alleviates ulcerative colitis (UC) via Th17/Treg cell homeostasis and TLR1-2/NF-κB signaling. Using DSS-induced UC mice, AG reduced inflammation, improved colon pathology, and restored Th17/Treg balance. Molecular analyses confirmed AG targets TLR1-TLR2 heterodimers to inhibit NF-κB activation, suggesting a mechanism for UC treatment.",
  "key_findings": [
    "AG reduced pro-inflammatory cytokines (IL-1β, TNF-α, IL-6) and improved colon histopathology in DSS-induced UC mice",
    "AG restored Th17/Treg cell balance through NF-κB signaling pathway inhibition",
    "AG targets TLR1-TLR2 heterodimers to modulate NF-κB nuclear translocation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies a specific molecular pathway (TLR1-2/NF-κB) by which a traditional Chinese medicine alleviates ulcerative colitis, advancing mechanistic understanding of immunomodulatory therapies for inflammatory bowel disease."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the demographic origins of Celtic languages using ancient genomic data from 4,587 Bronze and Iron Age European individuals. By analyzing population structure, it identifies three key processes: Steppe-related ancestry introduction via Bell Beaker groups around 4400 BP, Bronze Age migration from southwestern Europe to Britain, and a westward expansion of eastern central European ancestry (3200-2800 BP) linked to Hallstatt and La Tène cultures. The findings suggest the eastern central European migration is most parsimonious for Celtic spread, though language shifts may not directly follow genetic patterns.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Steppe-related ancestry arrived via Bell Beaker groups around 4400 BP across Celtic-speaking regions",
    "Bronze Age migration from southwestern Europe to Britain occurred between 3800-3200 BP",
    "Eastern central European ancestry expanded westward from 3200-2800 BP, affecting France, the British Isles, northeastern Iberia, and Italy"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides genomic evidence supporting a specific demographic pathway for Celtic language dispersal in prehistoric Europe, refining models of how linguistic and genetic histories interacted during the Iron Age."
}

{
  "summary": "This study systematically characterized herpesvirus-autoantigen interactions using immunoglobulin G reactivity profiling against viral peptides and host proteins in two biobank cohorts. By identifying 4,943 FDR-significant associations across 106 autoantigens, it revealed virus-specific disease networks, including cytomegalovirus's role in multimorbid conditions and Epstein-Barr virus's convergence on autoimmune hubs. The findings provide a framework for understanding viral contributions to chronic autoimmune diseases.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of 4,94: FDR-significant herpesvirus-autoantigen associations across 106 autoantigens",
    "Cytomegalovirus formed the largest multimorbid disease network, while Epstein-Barr virus converged on pleiotropic autoimmune hubs",
    "Eleven autoantigens were predicted with >85% accuracy using viral reactivities, suggesting molecular mimicry potential"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a comprehensive herpesvirus-autoantigen-disease network atlas, advancing understanding of how viral infections may drive chronic autoimmune conditions through molecular mimicry and immune cross-reactivity."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the resurgence of an unpopular hypothesis connecting Alzheimer's disease to neuronal loss. Using historical analysis and scientific reevaluation, it demonstrates how this theory regained traction despite initial skepticism. The findings suggest a potential reevaluation of Alzheimer's pathophysiology, highlighting the importance of revisiting established concepts in neurodegenerative research.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The hypothesis linking Alzheimer's disease to neuronal loss was previously dismissed but has since regained scientific credibility",
    "The study employed historical analysis and reevaluation to demonstrate the hypothesis's resurgence",
    "The findings indicate a need to reconsider established concepts in Alzheimer's pathophysiology"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study contributes to understanding how scientific theories can be reevaluated and regain relevance despite prior dismissal, offering insights into the dynamics of hypothesis acceptance in neurodegenerative disease research."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines artificial cilia inspired by natural cilia's structure and functions. It outlines natural cilia's roles in fluid propulsion, particle removal, and sensory detection across human organs. The study details fabrication methods, actuation mechanisms, and applications in robotics, drug delivery, and sensing. It identifies key challenges in mimicking natural cilia's performance for future biomimetic systems.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Artificial cilia mimic natural cilia's roles in fluid propulsion and particle removal",
    "Primary cilia in epidermis and inner ear enable pressure and sound detection",
    "Fabrication strategies and actuation mechanisms enable applications in robotics and drug delivery"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review advances understanding of biomimetic cilia design by synthesizing structural, functional, and application insights for next-generation artificial ciliary systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This review reassesses the pro-tumor role of M2-like tumor-associated macrophages (TAMs) by evaluating functional evidence from in vitro studies. It examines phagocytosis, antigen processing, cross-presentation, and CD8+ T cell activation. Findings indicate that some CD206+ TAMs can cross-present tumor antigens and activate CD8+ T cells comparably to dendritic cells, correlating with improved outcomes. Conversely, other macrophages may promote immunosuppression. The study emphasizes that antigen fate and co-stimulatory context, not M1/M2 markers, determine functional outcomes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CD206+ tumor-associated macrophages can cross-present tumor antigens and activate CD8+ T cells at levels matching conventional dendritic cells",
    "These macrophages correlate with better clinical outcomes in specific contexts",
    "Antigen-presenting macrophages may either promote antitumor immunity or immunosuppression depending on co-stimulatory signals"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes that functional assays, not surface markers alone, are critical for determining the immunological role of tumor-associated macrophages in cancer."
}

{
  "summary": "This study evaluates the Lancet Commission's obesity classification framework against BMI-only methods using data from 844,108 adults across four global cohorts. It found BMI overestimates obesity in 1.2-3.1% and underestimates it in 5.2-8.6% of participants. The combined anthropometric definition increased obesity prevalence by 3.3-7.4% and showed clinical obesity (22.7-31.3% of total) carries significantly higher mortality risk than preclinical obesity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "BMI overestimates obesity prevalence by 1.2-3.1% and underestimates it by 5.2-8.6% across cohorts",
    "Combined anthropometric definition increased obesity prevalence by 3.3-7.4% relative to BMI-only classification",
    "Clinical obesity confers a hazard ratio of 1.69 for all-cause mortality versus 1.19 for preclinical obesity"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides robust evidence supporting a more precise obesity classification system that better identifies high-risk individuals and improves mortality risk stratification globally."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates brain organoids as potential computational systems, focusing on their efficiency in information processing. Researchers assessed organoid capabilities to determine if they can serve as viable computing platforms. The findings indicate brain organoids demonstrate significant processing efficiency, suggesting they could become powerful computational tools with further optimization.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Brain organoids exhibit high processing efficiency",
    "Organoids show potential as viable computational platforms",
    "Further optimization may enhance their utility for computing applications"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances understanding of brain organoids' computational potential, highlighting their efficiency as a foundation for future neuromorphic computing systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of scalable diamond nanowire production by developing a lithography-free top-down etching method. It produces high-aspect-ratio nanowires on various diamond substrates, including polycrystalline, single-crystal, and boron-doped diamond. The approach uses silver-initiated micromasking to enable anisotropic etching, resulting in functional applications in photonic sensing, electrocatalysis, and pollutant degradation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "High-aspect-ratio diamond nanowires fabricated across multiple diamond substrate types via scalable, lithography-free etching",
    "Silver-initiated redeposition-sustained micromasking enables anisotropic etching for nanowire formation",
    "BDD nanowires show a 30-fold increase in electrochemical accessible surface area and 2.5-fold improvement in pollutant degradation kinetics"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a scalable pathway for integrating diamond nanostructures into advanced photonic and electrochemical applications without conventional lithography constraints."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated sustained autoantigen delivery for T1D immunotherapy using injectable hydrogel depots co-delivering insulin autoantigen and low-dose IL-2. The approach created transient tolerogenic niches that recruited regulatory T cells, delaying diabetes onset in non-obese diabetic mice from . The findings indicate that controlled antigen exposure in specific immune environments can induce durable immune tolerance.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Injectable hydrogel depots provided sustained co-delivery of insulin autoantigen and low-dose IL-2",
    "Transient tolerogenic niches recruited and expanded regulatory T cells in lymph nodes and spleen",
    "Median time to diabetes onset increased from 20 to >40 weeks in non-obese diabetic mice"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that sustained autoantigen exposure within transient inflammatory niches can induce durable immune tolerance in T1D, advancing strategies for antigen-specific immunotherapy."
}
